From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:42:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 06/78] Inline calls of SEH finally blocks in the parent's
 context (#41842)

On x86_64-win64, finally blocks become exception-filter procedures
that share the parent's tempgen; the parent initializes and finalizes
the managed temps they allocate. Since inlining moved to
TransformNodeTree, calls in a finally block are inlined only when the
filter is generated during the parent's pass 2, so a managed temp from
an inlined body sets pi_needs_implicit_finally after the parent has
decided not to use an implicit finally, giving internal error
200405231. Inline the filters' calls while transforming the parent and
propagate pi_needs_implicit_finally to it.
---
 compiler/psub.pas | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/compiler/psub.pas b/compiler/psub.pas
index 9e2ffaa4..c00093e8 100644
--- a/compiler/psub.pas
+++ b/compiler/psub.pas
@@ -1183,10 +1183,33 @@ implementation
         UserCode : TNode;
         updated,
         RedoDFA : boolean;
+        hpi : tcgprocinfo;
+        old_current_procinfo : tprocinfo;
       begin
        { inlining is a heuristics, so we do this very early }
        do_optinline(code,updated);
 
+       { The code of exception filters (SEH 'finally' blocks) is moved out of
+         this procedure before inlining takes place, and they share our
+         tempgen: we finalize the managed temps they allocate. Inline their
+         calls now, so that we know whether we need an implicit finally
+         before add_entry_exit_code decides on it (#41842) }
+       hpi:=tcgprocinfo(get_first_nestedproc);
+       while assigned(hpi) do
+         begin
+           if (hpi.procdef.proctypeoption=potype_exceptfilter) and
+              assigned(hpi.code) then
+             begin
+               old_current_procinfo:=current_procinfo;
+               current_procinfo:=hpi;
+               do_optinline(hpi.code,updated);
+               current_procinfo:=old_current_procinfo;
+               if pi_needs_implicit_finally in hpi.flags then
+                 include(flags,pi_needs_implicit_finally);
+             end;
+           hpi:=tcgprocinfo(hpi.next);
+         end;
+
        { do this before adding the entry code else the tail recursion recognition won't work,
          if this causes troubles, it must be if'ed
        }
